<title>INDIA: India 96/97 soymeal exports seen at 2.2 mln tonnes.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 soymeal exports seen at 2.2 mln tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's soymeal exports in the 1996/97 (Nov-Oct) season is expected to dip to 2.2 million tonnes from 2.6 million in the previous year, a senior official of the Soybean Processors Association of India (SOPA) said on Monday.  </p>
<p>&quot;Soymeal exports in the current season is expected to be about 2.2 million tonnes,&quot; Davish Jain, chairman of SOPA, told Reuters by telephone from the central Indian city of Indore.</p>
<p>Indore in Madhya Pradesh state is the hub of the country's soybean industry.</p>
<p>&quot;The fall in exports is expected due to a dip in output in the current season,&quot; Jain said. He said soybean output in the 1996/97 season was expected to fall to about four million tonnes from 4.45 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
